From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:40:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/apple-dart: Admit the J604's retained display at boot

The T8132 retained internal display (the DCP firmware DART at
0x30a340000 and the scanout/PIODMA frontend DART at 0x30a300000) stays
untouched until apple_dart.j713_dcp and apple_dart.j713_display are set.
That opt-in is the J713's guarded bring-up contract, and the J604 shares
it through apple_dart_retained_display_boards. So the J604 display came
up on appledrm only with both parameters on the kernel command line,
which an Omarchy install does not carry; without them it stays on the
boot framebuffer (simpledrm).

The J604 has run that path at boot on every kernel since -11.2 (MEASURED:
IOMFB startup 4.8 s, one DRM card, eDP-1 3024x1964@120, s2idle 4/4 with
the display back after each wake). Make it the board's default: a
second per-board list admits the retained display DARTs at probe without
the parameters. Everything after the gate is unchanged: the frontend
mappings and the DCP handoff are still validated, and without a complete
handoff from the loader the DCP and frontend are refused and the boot
framebuffer stays. The J713 keeps its opt-in, and the parameters still
work on both boards.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 .../boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-display.dtsi    |  9 +++++----
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c                    | 20 ++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-display.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-display.dtsi
index a02e39b393..bf7a946aa3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-display.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-display.dtsi
@@ -6,10 +6,11 @@
  * against the J604 Apple device tree (25G83 and 26B123 j604ap templates).
  * DCP-<id> tags name rows of DT-VERIFY-dcp.tsv.
  *
- * The DCP, its mailbox and its firmware DART are live when Linux starts. The
- * DART driver leaves both display DARTs untouched until apple_dart.j713_dcp or
- * apple_dart.j713_display is set, and appledrm adopts the inherited session
- * after guarded DART admission (same contract as t8132-j713-display.dtsi).
+ * The DCP, its mailbox and its firmware DART are live when Linux starts. On
+ * the J604 the DART driver admits both display DARTs at boot (the J713 waits
+ * for apple_dart.j713_dcp and apple_dart.j713_display), and appledrm adopts
+ * the inherited session after that guarded admission (same handoff contract
+ * as t8132-j713-display.dtsi).
  *
  * The boot loader completes these nodes: on dcp it publishes
  * apple,firmware-uuid, -version and -compat and the DCP firmware
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index a4edadf777..2784d634fa 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -3936,6 +3936,24 @@ static bool apple_dart_retained_display_board(void)
 	return of_machine_compatible_match(apple_dart_retained_display_boards);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Retained-display boards whose display DARTs are admitted at boot, without
+ * the j713_dcp and j713_display opt-in that the J713 keeps for its guarded
+ * bring-up. The J604 has started its DCP and scanout frontend from the
+ * loader's handoff on every boot since that path was qualified on it. The
+ * handoff checks are unchanged: without a complete handoff from the loader
+ * the frontend and DCP are refused and the boot framebuffer stays.
+ */
+static const char *const apple_dart_display_boot_admit_boards[] = {
+	"apple,j604",
+	NULL
+};
+
+static bool apple_dart_display_admitted_at_boot(void)
+{
+	return of_machine_compatible_match(apple_dart_display_boot_admit_boards);
+}
+
 /*
  * Boards whose loader leaves the MTP (keyboard and trackpad) coprocessor
  * running with every stream of its T8110 DART at 0x394800000 in bypass.
@@ -3977,7 +3995,7 @@ static int apple_dart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (j713_display && !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_APPLE_DART_J713_DCP))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EOPNOTSUPP,
 				     "retained J713 display requires CONFIG_APPLE_DART_J713_DCP=y\n");
-	if (j713_display &&
+	if (j713_display && !apple_dart_display_admitted_at_boot() &&
 	    ((res->start == 0x30a300000ULL && !READ_ONCE(apple_dart_frontend_enabled)) ||
 	     (res->start == 0x30a340000ULL && !READ_ONCE(apple_dart_dcp_enabled)))) {
 		dev_info(dev, "Leaving inherited display DART untouched; explicit guarded probe required\n");
